              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria' fontsize='12'>Summary Points</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Average vehicle value varies considerably across car types. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Panel Trucks have the highest average BLUEBOOK value among the car types. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria' fontsize='12'>Insights</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Vehicle type is an important factor in determining the underlying vehicle value. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Married customers (MSTATUS = Yes) form the majority across the different car types. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria' fontsize='12'>Recommendations</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Consider vehicle type and BLUEBOOK value when designing coverage and pricing strategies. </run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Cambria'>Use marital status along with vehicle and customer characteristics for more detailed customer segmentation.</run>
            </formatted-text>
